  An active AWS account with permissions to use Amazon SES (IAM user with SES and credential management rights).
​

Amazon SES configured in a chosen region (for you, ap-south-1/Mumbai is usually best for Kolkata).
​

At least one verified sender identity (email or domain) in SES that will be used as DEFAULT_FROM_EMAIL / SERVER_EMAIL.
​

SES SMTP credentials (SMTP username and password) generated for that region.
​

SES SMTP endpoint and port noted, for example email-smtp.<region>.amazonaws.com with port 587 or 465.
​

(Recommended) SES account moved out of Sandbox if you need to send to unverified recipient emails.
  ---------------------------------------
Outbound internet access

EC2 / EKS nodes must allow outbound traffic on:

TCP 587 (SMTP TLS) or 465 (SMTP SSL)

✅ AWS Account Prerequisites

Active AWS account

SES available in selected region (e.g., ap-south-1)

IAM permissions to:

Create users

Attach policies

Access SES

AWS SES enabled in target region

Region selected should match CVAT deployment region (recommended)

SES production access (important)

SES must be out of sandbox

Production access request approved

✅ Email / Domain Prerequisites

Verified email address or domain in SES

At least one verified sender:

noreply@yourdomain.com or

Individual email (for testing)

DNS access (for domain verification)

Ability to add:

TXT (verification)

CNAME (DKIM)

Via Route 53 or external DNS provider

✅ IAM & Security Prerequisites

IAM user or role for SES

Programmatic access enabled

Minimum permissions:

ses:SendEmail

ses:SendRawEmail

SMTP credentials created

SES SMTP username

SES SMTP password

Secure secret storage

Ability to store credentials using:

.env file (EC2)

Kubernetes Secret

AWS Secrets Manager (optional)

